  "parameterInterpretation": {
    "direct": "The covered primitive forward path passes first word to shape userdata+0, second word to +4, shifted low flag byte to +8 and secondary flag to +12. Getter candidate bodies resolve the same userdata helper and return the option dword or surface byte. Candidate API registration and live runtime values remain separate.",
    "exact": "Metadata enum defaults are authenticated independently from native shape-userdata source/return operands. All raw parameter words remain preserved. Aliased enum values retain every label.",
    "conditional": "Shared descriptor parameter order is applied as a stored default-decoder interpretation; complex-mesh activation and actual per-shape assignment remain separate.",
    "unresolved": "High packed flag bits beyond the shifted byte, arbitrary future enum values, semantic tag-config hash lookup and live callback/branch selection.",
    "complexMesh": "The optional complex record consumes one ordered mesh slot. Its source flags shift right by one for the surface byte, not two. The covered entry has no packed bit-zero attachment test; mesh ID validation, allocation and later runtime ownership remain conditional. Do not classify its clear bit zero as a disabled shape."
  }
